;; The print level's divergences (doc/C23-SURVEY.md, "As built: C3b"; bin/repr-c roundtrip): the classes of
;; test/repr/c/roundtrip-known.edn, in test/goi/divergences.edn's format (C8, generated from its :classes). A case is "corpus file", its
;; reason "known CLASS: the class's text".
;; No class takes `unclassified`, the placeholder an older --record gave a new failing file: bin/reap reports such a file as
;; in no class (queue 122); since 2026-11-02 --record writes none (it prints the file and fails). Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 ;; round 54: tcc-pp's 12.S and 13.S, assembler sources, out of cc-grammar (deferred) as the read level classes them; a guard class since
 ;; 2026-11-22 (c-tails): the round trip reads an assembler source as an assembler unit (SPEC §9.6), both pass levels 1 and 2 (and gcc's
 ;; level 3 by hand, the oracle tier's: the objects equal)
 {:id :assembler
  :title "an assembler source (.S), no C translation unit"
  :kind :design
  :why "an assembler source (.S), which gcc preprocesses as assembler-with-cpp and assembles: no C translation unit to read, print and compile; the port's C parser refuses it (tcc-pp's 12.S, 13.S), as the read level's class (CS260 (a)) holds its lexing"
  :decided "CS260 (a)'s rule at the print level, taken (round 54)"
  :match [#"^known assembler:"]}
 {:id :cc-grammar
  :title "the reference accepts the file, the port's parser (cc's, C3's trees) does not"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the reference accepts the file, the port's parser (cc's, C3's trees) does not: C23's attributes in positions cc's grammar lacks, the parenthesized storage-class compound literal, _Decimal64x, a declaration gcc's dialect takes (CS40 (a)'s rule; deferred to C4 and C7, CS80)"
  :decided "CS80 (a); C8"
  :match [#"^known cc-grammar:"]}
 {:id :converter-gap
  :title "a construct the converter does not write or writes losing a part"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "a construct the converter does not write or writes losing a part: an octal _BitInt or d32 suffix, a function defined through a typedef or auto, __declspec, an empty literal's digits, an attribute list after a declarator's comma, nullptr as a case label's operand (CS83), C2y's if and switch declarations, read as a block that declares them and printed as that block (CS194 (a))"
  :decided "CS83 (a); C8"
  :match [#"^known converter-gap:"]}
 {:id :eval-limits
  :title "the evaluated port's limits (CS60, CS78)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the evaluated port's limits (CS60, CS78): a recursion deeper than the evaluator's 10,000 calls (a stack overflow), or a read past the round trip's budget (REPR_C_READ_BUDGET, 120 s; a third of it for the :full read's): deferred until C5 compiles repr/c"
  :decided "CS60 (a), CS78 (a); C8"
  :match [#"^known eval-limits:"]}
 {:id :macro-context
  :title "a recovered invocation or a printed expansion means another thing where the print stands"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "a recovered invocation or a printed expansion means another thing where the print stands: a name a later function-like macro takes (the original's tokens hidden from it), an invocation's stringized escapes and spacing (CS82); since 2026-11-18 (CS82 (b), round 52) a callee an expansion hid from its function-like macro is printed parenthesized and a concatenated literal's run of invocations recovered whole (macro-skip-expand.c, stringify.c, 921227-1.c pass); since queue 540 (2026-11-23) an invocation whose expansion holds __LINE__ is printed as itself after `#line N /*arbace*/`, so shell.c's asserts no longer bring musl's stderr back expanded (its levels 1-2 pass, its level 3 is :objects'): a guard class"
  :decided "CS82 (b) in C5, (a) until then (the user, 2026-10-30): a fix planned; deferred (the user, 2026-11-02, queue 122 F5); CS82 (b) built, taken overnight (round 52)"
  :match [#"^known macro-context:"]}
 ;; a guard class since 2026-11-21 (c-rows): its two files' difference was the converter dropping a function declaration's asm label
 ;; (the print's object called memcpy, not my_memcpy); kept with the label, both pass level 3
 {:id :objects
  :title "the print is the same program (levels 1, 2, 4) but gcc -O0's object code differs: an asm label's section"
  :kind :design
  :why "the print is the same program (levels 1, 2, 4) but gcc -O0's object code differs by an asm label's section (builtins/memops-asm.c, strstr-asm.c): CS81 (a), level 4 the judge for them"
  :decided "CS81 (a) for the rest (the user, 2026-10-30)"
  :match [#"^known objects:"]}
 ;; DECISION 540-2 (the user, 2026-11-23): shell.c's level-3 difference is n/a, not by design
 {:id :objects-layout
  :title "the print is the same program (levels 1, 2) but gcc -O0's object code differs by a statement's layout"
  :kind :na
  :why "sqlite's shell.c (queue 540): the original's one-line `if( zCol==0 ) continue;` the :lines print lays over two lines, and gcc -O0's branches follow the lines (idxGetTableInfo, then idxFindCompatible when that line is joined by hand); no macro effect: the print is the same program at levels 1 and 2, and sqlite is no run corpus, so level 4 cannot judge"
  :decided "DECISION 540-2 (the user, 2026-11-23): n/a; alternatives not taken: by design as CS81 (a)'s rest; the :lines print keeping a jump on its if's line (line facts in the forms, a printer change, every corpus's level 3 again)"
  :match [#"^known objects-layout:"]}
 {:id :objects-macro-body
  :title "the print is the same program (levels 1, 2, 4) but gcc -O0's object code differs: code an invocation made"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "gcc -O0 gives every token of one expansion the invocation's location, and drops the nop before a body's end when its last statement and its brace share it; since 2026-11-06 (CS274 (a)) the print writes an invocation that made several top-level items or several statements of a list as the invocation itself (:c/macro-stmt on the first form, :c/macro-part on the rest), and 24 of the 26 files pass; since 2026-11-18 (CS82 (b), round 52) a statement an invocation made but for its `;` (NEEDBITS(16);) and an invocation inside an asm's operands (__FUNCTION__) printed as the invocation: inflate.c and pr27528.c pass; since queue 540 (2026-11-23) an invocation whose expansion holds __LINE__ (an assert) is printed as itself after `#line N /*arbace*/`, and unicode_gen.c's last `assert(0);` keeps its object (the VM's aarch64 gcc, level 3 by hand): left until the main host's gcc record (amd64) shows it, then a guard class"
  :decided "CS81 (b) for the bodies an invocation made (the user, 2026-10-30; queue 122 F5); CS274 (a) (the user, 2026-11-06)"
  :match [#"^known objects-macro-body:"]}
 {:id :print-grammar
  :title "the :lines print holds what cc's grammar (the reread) or gcc refuses though the original did not"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the :lines print holds what cc's grammar (the reread) or gcc refuses though the original did not: an attribute leading a type name, a recovered invocation of a pp-number with a UCN, a ref to #embed's resource the print's directory lacks (CS80)"
  :decided "CS80 (a); C8"
  :match [#"^known print-grammar:"]}
 {:id :reexpansion
  :title "a macro invocation inside a larger one is printed expanded, and reexpanded by the reread"
  :kind :design
  :why "a macro invocation inside a larger one (not a whole node) is printed expanded, and a self-referential macro of the expansion (musl's #define stdout (stdout)) is expanded again by the reread: the forms gain the inner invocation's :c/macro (N6's limit; the objects equal)"
  :decided "CS262 (a); C8"
  :match [#"^known reexpansion:"]}
 ;; a guard class since 2026-11-21 (c-rows): level 4 judges a print only where level 3 (the objects byte for byte) does not hold it
 ;; already (arbace.repr.c.rtcheck's judge-row); return-addr.c and reverse-complement-5.c, objects equal, pass
 {:id :run-address
  :title "the original and the print run differently though their objects are equal"
  :kind :design
  :why "the original and the print run differently though their objects are equal: the program prints addresses (return-addr.c), a run's own nondeterminism"
  :decided "CS262 (a); C8"
  :match [#"^known run-address:"]}
 ;; a guard class since 2026-11-06 (CS275 (a)): the six self-including files pass
 {:id :self-include
  :title "the main file includes itself (#include __FILE__-like tests)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the main file includes itself (#include __FILE__-like tests): refused until 2026-11-06; since CS275 (a) the read takes the re-entered copy as a file of its own (the preprocessor's *reentry*, bound by every read-c), its #include printed where it stands, and an executed conditional family's groups the main pass skipped printed as their text (a c/directive), so that the print's own second pass takes them"
  :decided "CS261 (a): deferred, the converter to read the re-entered main file as an include of its own (the user, 2026-11-02, queue 122 F5)"
  :match [#"^known self-include:"]}
 ;; a guard class since 2026-11-18 (CS329 (a)): its last two files left it
 {:id :split-declaration
  :title "a declaration begins in one file and ends in another (SPEC §4.3's split-declaration)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "a declaration begins in one file and ends in another (SPEC §4.3's split-declaration): refused; since 2026-11-06 (CS275 (a)) not when every other file's token comes from an #include the declaration holds between the items of a statement list (the print writes the #include there: 18_include, zlib's infback and inflate); since 2026-11-18 (CS329 (a), round 52) not when it is held between the elements of an initializer or an enumerator list either (the #include and the directives around it elements of the list's forms, printed on their own lines: quickjs's libregexp.c passes, unicode_gen.c reaches level 3, objects-macro-body: an assert printed expanded for its __LINE__); a guard class"
  :decided "CS104 (a): the converter keeps such a declaration whole (C6); deferred as at eval (the user, 2026-11-02, queue 122 F5)"
  :match [#"^known split-declaration:"]}
]
